  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4) \\\\  & =8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-3\\cdot 2x-12\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =24{x}^{2}-6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{\u2032}(x)=6$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24{x}^{2}-6x-12 & =6 \\\\ 24{x}^{2}-6x-18 & =0 \\\\ 6(4{x}^{2}-x-3) & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)(4x+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $6$ at the point where $x=1$ and $x=-\\frac{3}{4}.$ Since $x>0$, our answer is $x=1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
